  "research": {
    "summary": "Current work analyzes large-scale energy, water, climate, and urban resource systems to inform technically, politically, and socially consequential decisions. Recent priorities include grid resilience and winter load growth, localized heat from data centers and other anthropogenic sources, air-conditioning access and health outcomes, residential smart-meter analysis, urban heat inequity, household outage disparities, renewable-energy and electrification pathways, and AI-supported solar mapping.",
